# Lesson UI

Lesson screens use the Duolingo tile: white, `rounded-2xl`, `border-2 border-b-4 border-[#e5e5ea]`, bold text, one column on a phone. No sideways scrolling.

- Align the lesson to the top. Do not center it in the leftover viewport.
- Weiter reveals one new piece of the same slide. Earlier pieces stay. A new slide is a new scene.
- Words a student reads are Vietnamese. German is the sentence being taught. Do not style a teaching line like an error or a system alert.
- A highlighted word is a thick underscore in its own color (`underline decoration-[3px]`), not a filled chip.
